    "summary": "Indigo gown (boubou, tobe), composed of a single width of European calico cotton, forming a rectangle. A slit has been cut into the centre for the wearer’s head. With the exception of the area surrounded the slit and the two ends, the cloth has been covered with wax into which streaks have been drawn with a comb. After dying in an indigo bath, this produces a combed area of white and light blue against ends and neck area of dark blue.",
